    <section class="relative py-20 bg-slate-900 text-white overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[url('/attached_assets/planexus-messe-analytica-2026-muenchen_1770786130636.png')] bg-cover bg-center opacity-20"></div>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-slate-900 via-slate-900/90 to-slate-900/70"></div>
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 relative z-10">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
            <span class="bg-primary/20 text-primary px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full text-sm font-medium flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="4" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="16" x2="16" y1="2" y2="6"/><line x1="8" x2="8" y1="2" y2="6"/><line x1="3" x2="21" y1="10" y2="10"/></svg>
              Trade fairs &amp; events
            </span>
            <span class="text-gray-400 text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
              10 min read
            </span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold mb-6 leading-tight">
            Planexus at analytica 2026 — why your visit is essential
          </h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
            24–27 March 2026, Messe München · Hall B2, Stand 322 · Together with Wesemann
          </p>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-6 text-sm text-gray-400">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="4" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="16" x2="16" y1="2" y2="6"/><line x1="8" x2="8" y1="2" y2="6"/><line x1="3" x2="21" y1="10" y2="10"/></svg>
              11 February 2026
            </span>
            <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/></svg>
              Sven Biewald
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-slate-50 border-b border-gray-100 py-4">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500">
          <a href="/en" class="hover:text-primary">Home</a>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
          <a href="/en/magazine" class="hover:text-primary">Magazine</a>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
          <span class="text-primary font-medium">Planexus at analytica 2026</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
          <div class="lg:col-span-8">
            <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                <strong>analytica</strong> in Munich has been the global focal point for laboratory technology, analytics and biotechnology since 1968. More than 1,200 exhibitors and around 40,000 trade visitors from more than 120 countries come together every two years at the Messe München exhibition centre. The 2026 edition, however, takes place under quite particular circumstances: the industry is under pressure to become faster, more sustainable and more digital. Classic laboratory planning — years of lead time, rigid rooms, little scope for adaptation — can no longer keep pace with the speed of research.
              </p>

              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                This is precisely where <a href="/en/about" class="text-primary hover:underline">Planexus</a> comes in. At analytica 2026 we set out to show that modular construction is far more than a substitute for solid building — it is the foundation for the laboratory innovation of tomorrow. Together with our partner <strong>Wesemann</strong>, one of the leading manufacturers of laboratory installations, we present in <strong>Hall B2, Stand 322</strong> the interplay of modular building structure and professional laboratory equipment.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-primary/5 border border-primary/20 rounded-xl p-6 my-8 not-prose">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                  <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-lg p-3 flex-shrink-0">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="4" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="16" x2="16" y1="2" y2="6"/><line x1="8" x2="8" y1="2" y2="6"/><line x1="3" x2="21" y1="10" y2="10"/></svg>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-lg mb-2">analytica 2026 — the facts</h4>
                    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-1">
                      <li><strong>Dates:</strong> 24–27 March 2026</li>
                      <li><strong>Venue:</strong> Messe München, Am Messesee 2, 81829 Munich</li>
                      <li><strong>Planexus stand:</strong> Hall B2, Stand 322 (together with Wesemann)</li>
                      <li><strong>Opening hours:</strong> Tue–Thu 09:00–17:00, Fri 09:00–16:00</li>
                      <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.analytica.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">www.analytica.de</a></li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                Why analytica 2026 will be a distinctive edition
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                The laboratory industry is undergoing a profound shift. Three megatrends dominate the discussion at this year’s analytica: digitalisation, sustainability and speed. Research institutions are under pressure to deliver results faster. Pharmaceutical companies must build new production capacity in months rather than years. And the entire industry must reduce its ecological footprint — without compromising quality.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                analytica addresses these themes deliberately. Alongside the classic exhibition, the accompanying <strong>analytica conference</strong> offers a scientific programme of the highest calibre. For Planexus the fair is the platform to show how <a href="/en/services/modular-construction" class="text-primary hover:underline">modular laboratory construction</a> answers all three challenges at once.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                1. Modular flexibility as a strategic advantage
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                The days when laboratory planning took years and rooms stayed rigid for decades are over. Modern research needs speed. A new project requires a new laboratory environment — and not in 24 months, but in 24 weeks. Our <a href="/en/services" class="text-primary hover:underline">lab container solutions</a> offer the decisive advantage here.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl my-8 not-prose">
                <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">What modular construction means in practice</h4>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
                  <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-100">
                    <div class="text-primary font-bold text-lg mb-1">Rapid availability</div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">From <a href="/en/services/planning" class="text-primary hover:underline">3D planning</a> to commissioning in record time. Standard configurations are ready within 4–8 weeks.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-100">
                    <div class="text-primary font-bold text-lg mb-1">Scalability</div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Laboratories that grow with your requirements. Modules can be added, reconfigured or relocated to new sites.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-100">
                    <div class="text-primary font-bold text-lg mb-1">Turnkey</div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Fully equipped modules, delivered worldwide and <a href="/en/services/logistics" class="text-primary hover:underline">installed turnkey</a>. Plug-and-play instead of a permanent construction site.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                At analytica 2026 we show you live how we translate complex requirements into modular structures — without compromising quality. Whether <a href="/en/magazine/bsl-2-bsl-3-container-lab" class="text-primary hover:underline">BSL-2 and BSL-3 containment laboratories</a>, <a href="/en/magazine/gmp-cleanroom-container-pharma-production" class="text-primary hover:underline">GMP-compliant cleanrooms</a> or classic analytical laboratories: every project begins with individual <a href="/en/services/consulting" class="text-primary hover:underline">consulting</a> and a tailored design.
              </p>

              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                The advantage over classic solid construction is not only speed. Modular laboratories can be relocated, extended or dismantled — your investment remains flexible. That is particularly relevant for companies evaluating sites, running research projects with a limited duration or needing to respond quickly to regulatory change.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                2. Smart Lab integration: think. plan. connect.
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Under our motto “Connect” we mean not only the physical joining of modules, but above all digital networking. The <a href="/en/services/smart-lab" class="text-primary hover:underline">Smart Lab</a> is one of the top themes at analytica 2026 — and a field in which Planexus brings genuine expertise. We integrate the latest IoT technologies directly into the laboratory structure, not as a later add-on but as an integral part of the design.
              </p>

              <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
                Real-time monitoring
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Temperature, humidity, particle concentration, differential pressure — in a modern laboratory these parameters must not only be maintained, but documented without gaps. Our Smart Lab solutions enable monitoring of all relevant environmental conditions in real time. Deviations are detected and reported immediately, before they become a problem. For GMP environments this kind of documentation is not optional; it is a prerequisite for qualification.
              </p>

              <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
                Future-proof infrastructure
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                A laboratory built today must still work in five years — probably with technologies that do not yet exist. That is why we plan the digital infrastructure so that it can be extended. Empty conduits for data cables, open interfaces for building automation, preparation for AI-supported automation processes. Those who build smart today save conversion costs tomorrow.
              </p>

              <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
                Efficiency through intelligent use of space
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Modular laboratories have inherently limited floor areas. That is not a disadvantage — it is a design principle. Every square metre is considered, every work surface optimised. Wesemann’s <a href="/en/services/equipment" class="text-primary hover:underline">laboratory equipment</a> complements our spatial planning perfectly: laboratory benches, fume cupboards, media columns and safety installations are matched exactly to the container geometry.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                3. Sustainability meets high-tech
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Sustainability is the focus theme of analytica 2026 — and modular construction is by nature more resource-efficient than conventional methods. That is not a marketing claim, but a consequence of the manufacturing approach.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl my-8 not-prose">
                <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Sustainability in modular laboratory construction</h4>
                <div class="space-y-4">
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-full p-1 mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Reduced material waste</p>
                      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Industrial prefabrication in the workshop means precise cutting, minimal offcuts and controlled conditions. Compared with site operations, up to 80% less waste is generated.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-full p-1 mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Reusability</p>
                      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Modules can be deployed at new sites instead of being demolished. A lab container no longer needed at site A can begin a second life at site B.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-full p-1 mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Energy efficiency</p>
                      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Use of the latest insulation and building technology in our specialised containers. Heat recovery, LED lighting and intelligent climate control are standard, not extras.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-full p-1 mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">Shorter build time = less CO₂</p>
                      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Less site traffic, shorter journeys for trades, reduced on-site plant use. Prefabrication in the factory reduces the site phase to a minimum.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                In practice that means: a modular laboratory can be significantly more sustainable in the overall balance than a conventional new build. Particularly when the entire life cycle is considered — from manufacture via operation through to possible dismantling or relocation to a new site. You can read more on this in our article <a href="/en/magazine/sustainability-lab-construction-energy-efficiency" class="text-primary hover:underline">Sustainability in laboratory construction: energy efficiency meets high-tech</a>.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                4. What to expect at our stand
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                We warmly invite you to become part of this transformation. Visit us together with our partner Wesemann at <strong>Stand 322 in Hall B2</strong>.
              </p>

              <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl my-8 not-prose">
                <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">At the stand you can expect</h4>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-full p-1 mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Reference projects:</strong> Insights into current projects from pharma, research and industry — with images, data and practical experience.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-full p-1 mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Personal consulting:</strong> From a single container to a large research centre — our experts advise you on your individual project.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-full p-1 mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Smart Lab demonstrations:</strong> Experience live how IoT monitoring and digital networking work in a modular laboratory.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                    <div class="bg-primary/20 rounded-full p-1 mt-1 flex-shrink-0">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-primary"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Laboratory furniture from Wesemann:</strong> Laboratory benches, fume cupboards and furniture perfectly matched to modular structures.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">
                5. Planexus and Wesemann: modular construction and laboratory fit-out from a single source
              </h2>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                The joint presence at analytica is no coincidence. Planexus belongs to <a href="/en/partners" class="text-primary hover:underline">Wesemann Holding GmbH</a>. That means: when you commission a modular laboratory with us, you receive not only the building structure but also the complete laboratory fit-out from a single source. No interface problem between building and furniture design, no coordination gaps between different trades.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
